flowchart LR
accTitle: Separate forward, return, and outbound traffic cases
accDescr: Three separate cases show vWAN Firewall egress, workload-subnet NAT egress, and private endpoint access. Every case shows a return path. NAT is not an override for a route to a virtual appliance.
subgraph A["Case A — secured hub profile"]
direction LR
A1["Spoke source"] -->|"Selected hub route"| A2["Hub + Firewall"]
A2 -->|"Policy + SNAT"| A3["Internet destination"]
A3 -.->|"Response to translated source"| A2
A2 -.->|"Reverse flow"| A1
end
subgraph B["Case B — subnet NAT egress"]
direction LR
B1["Workload source"] -->|"Internet next hop"| B2["Associated NAT Gateway"]
B2 -->|"SNAT"| B3["Internet destination"]
B3 -.->|"Response"| B2
B2 -.->|"Reverse translation"| B1
end
subgraph C["Case C — private service"]
direction LR
C1["Authorized private client"] -->|"DNS yields endpoint IP"| C2["Route to private endpoint"]
C2 -->|"Approved service connection"| C3["Blob data plane"]
C3 -.->|"Authorized response"| C2
C2 -.->|"Return route"| C1
end
N["Each row is independent<br/>UDR to appliance changes the egress path<br/>DNS + route + policy + authorization all matter<br/>Live packet evidence: NOT RUN"]:::note
A3 ~~~ N
